// prompts.memql
//
// The ONE bounded model call this epic allows (design D6). It proposes a
// derivation for a hole the rules could not explain -- one that SOME recorded
// instances derive from an earlier result and some do not.
//
// The answer is not trusted. Whatever comes back is parsed against the closed
// grammar in component/procedure and then checked against EVERY instance; a
// proposal that explains some and not others is rejected and the hole stays a
// free parameter. So this prompt cannot make a procedure wrong -- at worst it
// costs one call and changes nothing.

/// Propose how one argument of a recorded procedure is derived from an earlier step's result.
/// Answers ONE expression in a closed grammar, or an empty string when nothing fits. The engine
/// checks the answer against every recorded instance before it is kept, so a guess costs a call and
/// nothing else.
@description("Propose a derivation expression for an unexplained hole in a learned procedure")
@level("reasoning")
@templateFile("deriveHole.tmpl")
prompt deriveProcedureHole {
  holePath   string   @required @description("Where the hole sits in the step's arguments, as a dotted path.")
  holeType   string   @description("The widest type observed at that position: string, number, bool, object, array or mixed.")
  instances  []object @required @description("One entry per recorded instance: {value, earlierResults}, where earlierResults is a list of {stepIndex, path, value} the procedure's earlier steps produced.")
}
